+## Visible alert mode (optional)
+
+By default every wake is a silent background push (APNs `content-available`,
+FCM data-only) and the device wakes to drain its mediator. On iOS that is best
+effort:
+
+> "the system may throttle the delivery of background notifications if the
+> total number becomes excessive. The number of background notifications
+> allowed by the system depends on current conditions, but don't try to send
+> more than two or three per hour."
+>
+> "If something force quits or kills the app, the system discards the held
+> notification."
+>
+> — Apple, [Pushing background updates to your App](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/usernotifications/pushing-background-updates-to-your-app)
+
+A wake that a person is waiting on, such as an approval, cannot depend on that.
+With `GATEWAY_ALERT_LOC_KEY` set, an **interactive** wake (`urgency:
+interactive`) is sent as a notification the platform displays itself, in any
+app state:
+
+| | Silent (default, and every background wake) | Visible (interactive wake, mode on) |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| APNs | `apns-push-type: background`, priority 5, `aps.content-available` | `apns-push-type: alert`, priority 10, `apns-collapse-id`, `aps.alert.loc-key` (+ `title-loc-key`), `sound`, `thread-id`, still `content-available` |
+| FCM | data-only, `android.priority: high` | the same data, plus `android.notification` (`body_loc_key`, `title_loc_key`, `channel_id`, `tag`) and `android.collapse_key` |
+
+It stays contentless in the binding's sense: the payload names a
+**localisation key**, never text, and the device shows its own string for it.
+Apple: "If the text of your notification messages is predetermined, you can
+store your message strings in the Localizable.strings file of your app bundle
+and use the title-loc-key, subtitle-loc-key, and loc-key payload keys"
+([Generating a remote notification](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/usernotifications/generating-a-remote-notification)).
+On Android, `body_loc_key` names a string resource in the app. The wake's hint
+fields ride along unchanged, and no app extension is needed. Using one key for
+every wake means the push services see a wake, not what kind it was.
+
+Keys, the collapse id and the channel id must be `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`; an invalid
+value stops startup.
+
 ## Testing Web Push end-to-end
 
 The wake loop spans the gateway, a VTA + mediator, and the browser plugin. A
